values ('b9f4d2e7-6c38-4a15-8b29-2e1d7c5a6f48', 'lifecycle-nutrition', 'Lifecycle Nutrition', 'This course examines nutritional requirements, feeding relationships, dietary patterns, assessment, counseling, and public-health context from preconception through older adulthood. Students integrate physiology and development with culture, family systems, food access, disability, activity, chronic-disease risk, and care settings. Cases emphasize safe, evidence-informed, culturally responsive planning within the undergraduate dietetics scope, including recognition of red flags requiring referral or medical nutrition therapy.');

