idance and high-risk referral"}, {"id": "9688257f-ca8c-4383-9750-4f74a3e9d2a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Choking versus gagging, texture progression, and safe seating"}, {"id": "dd9daee0-9647-48ec-b5b4-32221a0f1624", "type": "concept", "title": "Honey, unpasteurized foods, high-mercury fish, and foodborne-risk prevention"}]}]}, {"id": "bafcff98-bdd1-4a26-8b30-124f85c8b106", "type": "topic", "title": "Toddler and Preschool Nutrition", "description": "Focuses on autonomy, variable appetite, feeding skill development, family meals, and nutrient-dense patterns without pressure or moralizing food.", "children": [{"id": "9ce63fbe-5fcf-4785-b8bb-a02651a01aeb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Growth and appetite", "description": "Explain why appetite often varies as growth velocity changes.", "children": [{"id": "48f0004f-88b4-4684-a107-e0b6c03bf06f", "type": "concept", "title": "Portion expectations and appetite variability"}, {"id": "d6640a5d-369d-4cb8-8d20-9d2bab5568fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Iron, vitamin D, calcium, fiber, and beverage patterns"}, {"id": "122530ae-6988-49d4-abb3-aacd84e703ee", "type": "concept", "title": "Milk intake, juice, grazing, and constipation considerations"}]}, {"id": "30d80c81-2374-4b10-bc5d-3527f7dac3ea", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Feeding relationship", "description": "Use responsive structure that divides caregiver and child responsibilities appropriately.", "children": [{"id": "9860d9bb-4453-4c06-9ed0-9bfef1c0ab02", "type": "concept", "title": "Hunger/fullness cues and repeated neutral exposure"}, {"id": "59f253d9-1252-4bde-bd65-e1bd5589aa0d", "type": "concept", "title": "Food neophobia, sensory preferences, and routine"}, {"id": "ed29731d-601f-4ce8-9209-a140243088ff", "type": "concept", "title": "Pressure, restriction, rewards, and mealtime conflict"}]}, {"id": "fe1a5239-0af2-4735-a3c1-de8f165f8b7d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Development and safety", "description": "Adapt eating environments to skills, disability, and family context.", "children": [{"id": "cac83bdf-6c1b-4142-874f-1b09d78d6a7b", "type": "concept", "title": "Texture, utensils, oral-motor skills, and choking prevention"}, {"id": "b331a071-a50b-4fac-9891-9252c694c669", "type": "concept", "title": "Dental health and sugar exposure"}, {"id": "7296a265-0cc3-4abf-880c-eca758a7d66f", "type": "concept", "title": "Daycare, family culture, food allergy, and feeding-team referral"}]}]}, {"id": "16576695-96d0-4119-9547-95101e2b8cfd", "type": "topic", "title": "School-Age Child Nutrition", "description": "Connects growth and learning with breakfast, school food, family patterns, activity, sleep, and an increasingly independent food environment.", "children": [{"id": "293b28c0-47c3-4f78-bee4-5da0609e8e46", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Growth and nutrient needs", "description": "Support steady growth and development using longitudinal assessment.", "children": [{"id": "3722cd05-35b3-436d-95f0-02b268f0e774", "type": "concept", "title": "Energy balance without calorie fixation"}, {"id": "843dce7e-c0ac-4e1e-92de-43da6a8dad7f", "type": "concept", "title": "Calcium, vitamin D, iron, fiber, and hydration"}, {"id": "f7e160ee-afe8-41b0-9693-e596118f3eed", "type": "concept", "title": "Dental health, constipation, and common nutrient gaps"}]}, {"id": "4b2770a6-7e5a-4fa7-abd2-211a9f8b6dc0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "School and family environments", "description": "Evaluate how routines and systems influence intake.", "children": [{"id": "a3ba9107-0ec8-486c-ac2f-b1c232253eab", "type": "concept", "title": "Breakfast, packed meals, school meals, snacks, and after-school care"}, {"id": "991ced46-6967-48a1-824b-43d5daaa932f", "type": "concept", "title": "Marketing, screen use, sleep, and physical activity"}, {"id": "187fea45-57ee-4fd3-b529-ba3cd9c2ef59", "type": "concept", "title": "Food insecurity, school nutrition programs, and stigma-free access"}]}, {"id": "d8a32ce6-0fb3-4e45-a147-05f49b367b4d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Body image and inclusive care", "description": "Promote health without reinforcing weight bias or disordered eating.", "children": [{"id": "e8297ae9-f5c2-4288-8d5c-2a1d6042212a", "type": "concept", "title": "Weight-neutral communication and growth privacy"}, {"id": "1f2e8839-d62d-49a8-8156-5d2c1a016cc4", "type": "concept", "title": "Anti-diet literacy and media influence"}, {"id": "3870a91f-0958-45de-8d69-c0609b80fa6a", "type": "concept", "title": "Eating-disorder warning signs, bullying, and referral pathways"}]}]}, {"id": "c0dd3639-e6eb-459a-9f0b-eb01991c15ef", "type": "topic", "title": "Adolescent Nutrition and Transition to Adulthood", "description": "Addresses puberty, peak bone and lean-mass accrual, growing independence, sport, sleep, substance exposure, and heightened vulnerability to disordered eating.", "children": [{"id": "c60950d3-d8dd-4cb5-81cd-43aad5a33cdd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Puberty and requirements", "description": "Relate maturation and growth velocity to changing needs.", "children": [{"id": "0f7de155-8bd4-4af4-bf13-0be313ee5ea3", "type": "concept", "title": "Energy and protein variability"}, {"id": "a2b375d7-d62f-4110-889b-4172d6afcc90", "type": "concept", "title": "Iron, calcium, vitamin D, folate, zinc, and B12"}, {"id": "3bee969c-3cc0-41f4-ad90-eda9f4a90872", "type": "concept", "title": "Menstruation, bone accrual, and developmental timing"}]}, {"id": "f5afd6d7-85df-4fa8-bd92-b0563d5de5b4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Autonomy and environment", "description": "Support practical choices across school, work, peers, culture, and digital media.", "children": [{"id": "4a9788d7-1524-4b68-908c-f9ee257d374b", "type": "concept", "title": "Meal patterns, convenience foods, caffeine, and sugary drinks"}, {"id": "85d99668-6806-48d4-bc88-16eb0fc1439f", "type": "concept", "title": "Vegetarian/vegan diets and supplement oversight"}, {"id": "05c2e0b6-724f-47dd-80a6-716868e590b3", "type": "concept", "title": "Food skills, budgeting, and transition to independen